{"type":"after","callId":"call@471","endTime":54358.449,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/The USB serial console — QUERY and SETUP\n    \n\nThe USB serial console —  and \nThe micro-USB \"Programing Port\" is a Teensy serial console with two commands, not the  protocol and not SSH\n✅bench👥communityLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nThe BRX has two ports: charging, and a separate micro-USB \"Programing Port\". Plugged into a computer it enumerates as a Teensyduino USB Serial CDC device (Windows , macOS , Linux , VID ). Baud is ignored. This is what the community means by \"PuTTY into the tagger\". The command set came from LaserTagMods' headset-pairing note.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7c; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24 B7)\nWhat the port does and does not do\n\n\nSent\nResult\nConf\n\n\n\n, , any  frame\nEchoed back (local echo on — easy to mistake for a reply); with CR: \n✅bench\n\n\n, , , , …\n\n✅bench\n\n\n + CR\nDumps the device record (below). Case-insensitive.\n✅bench\n\n\n + CR\nEnters factory provisioning; prompts (EN/中文) for the headset's serial number\n✅bench\n\n\nHold SELECT while powering on with USB connected\nMass-storage mode exposing the on-board sound storage (the sound-pack update path) — a different mode from the console\n👥community\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7c; protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (\"New sounds ON THE TAGGER\")\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7c (values are one unit's; PIN/serial redacted)\nReal-format quirksthe parser has to survive:  is NUL-padded, lines end ,  can read  instead of a number,  is a real non-zero value.  ships  and , which saves a backup to .Source: docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24 B7); mcp/brx_mcp/protocol.py\n — the provisioning/re-pair path (identity lives here)\nRun  on both gun and headset-side records first;  on the gun asks for the headset's serial number — that is the gun↔headset pairing mechanism.\nThe \"Factory Defaults\" banner is a mode header, not an action: entering  and power-cycling out changed nothing (field-by-field diff).\n👥community The community's \"change tagger ID / re-pair the headset\" procedure is this console (LaserTagMods' headset-pairing note); the identity fields it concerns are the ones  prints: , , , .\nOnly the first prompt (the headset serial) has been walked on our bench. Do it only on a gun you can afford to re-pair.\nFor per-game identity you do not need this:  token 1 over BLE sets the player id each game.\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7c, §7p; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24)\nFirmware backup is impossible; do not reflash.Teensy's HalfKay bootloader is write-only by design, so no image can be read back. Rollback depends entirely on Battle Company supplying the original image. The official app's version gate (supports \"until v2.01e\") is an upper bound; it warns and still runs a game.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7b, §7c\nIs  over BLE the same thing?No. Over BLE it returns a -framed status array with no serial, PIN or version. The device record is USB-only.\nWhat is the advertised BLE name vs ?Two fields: the advertisement is  from the MAC tail;  is what  writes.\nSource: docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24) · docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24)\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@471"}
